Source-grounded routing hint from pre-screening:
Preserve only the source-backed leading asymptotic normalized localization-length family. Define q=W/W_ref and Y(q)=lim_(W_ref->0 at fixed finite q) xi(q W_ref)/xi(W_ref)=q^(-p), with a public finite benchmark interval q in [1,10]. Historical private chi=0.1 has p=2 and AST exponent negative_p=-2; alternate private chi=0.2 has p=4 and AST exponent negative_p=-4. The two oracle ASTs must be structurally identical power(q,negative_p), differing only in private negative_p. Keep weak-disorder and E=-1.8 conditions and exact source locators. Correct the prior support text: E=-2 cos(k)=-1.8 gives k=acos(0.9), 2k approximately 0.90205; at chi=0.1, k0=2 pi chi approximately 0.62832, hence k0<2k and S(2k)=1; at chi=0.2, k0 approximately 1.25664, hence 2k<k0<pi-k, the first-order term vanishes and the W^-4 second-order branch applies. Do not encode absolute localization coefficients, an unsupported W interval, finite-size numerical measurements, or extra claims. Treat q interval and normalization as benchmark-derived from the source asymptotic law, not directly reported measurements; source_ambiguities remains empty only if the selected cluster is source-unambiguous.
This hint only selects a part of the supplied source for inspection. Verify every extracted fact against that source and provide exact locators; the source remains the sole authority. If the hinted cluster is unsupported or incomplete, represent it faithfully and set case_authoring_ready false.

